# Add commands and live updates

**Prerequisites:** [First standalone app](/docs/tutorials/first-app/).
**You will learn:** when a one-shot `@patch` is enough, and when `@command` plus
`@live` justifies a shared stream.
**Starting files:** [Counter](/examples/counter/) and
[Live counter](/examples/live-counter/).
**Time:** about twenty minutes.
**Verify:** Datastar POST is empty SSE; `curl` POST is JSON; a second tab morphs on
the live app.
**Next:** [Take ownership with main.roc](/docs/tutorials/custom-main/).

Open both generated source pages:

- [Counter.rocci](/examples/counter/source/Counter-rocci/) — `@patch` returns
  `counterCard`
- [LiveCounter.rocci](/examples/live-counter/source/LiveCounter-rocci/) —
  `@command` returns `{ count }`, `@live` returns `counterCard`

## One-shot versus live

| | Counter | Live counter |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Mutation | `@patch` | `@command` |
| Acting tab | Morphs from the POST body | Receives **empty SSE**, no morph from POST |
| Other tabs | Stale until click/reload | Morph from `GET /sse` |
| Return value | Html fragment | Roc record |

Use one-shot when only the acting tab should change (search, click-to-edit,
validation). Use live when every open client should see the same region.
Do not patch the same `id` from both a command and the stream.

`@live` is one per module. Rocci generates `GET /sse` and injects
`data-init=@get("/sse", …)` on `<body>` when that attribute is absent. Do not
author `GET /sse` yourself in the same module.

## HTTP verification

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- run \
  examples/rocci/standalone/live-counter/LiveCounter.rocci --no-window
```

```sh
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/ | grep -E 'id="counter"|/sse'
curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/actions/counter/increment
# JSON {"count":N}
curl -s -D - -o /dev/null -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/actions/counter/increment \
  -H 'Datastar-Request: true'
# HTTP/1.1 200 OK  Content-Type: text/event-stream  (empty body / zero events)
```

**Verify:** ordinary clients get JSON; Datastar gets empty SSE (not 204). Open the printed URL
in two browsers: increment in one, the other `#counter` updates without a
reload. That two-client check is the definition of live for this tutorial.

JSON does **not** morph the DOM. Do not bind the visible count to `$count` to
reuse the command body.

## Ability checklist

- Choose `@patch` vs `@command` + `@live` for a given flow
- Discriminate Datastar with `Datastar-Request: true`, not `Accept`
- Explain why a second counter tab stays stale

Next: [custom main.roc](/docs/tutorials/custom-main/). Handler matrix (every
accepted form, not a beginner app): [Handler matrix](/examples/handler-matrix/).
